WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:11.880
I’ll come home later tonight.
I have a business meeting

2
00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:15.400
OK.

3
00:00:16.840 --> 00:00:20.080
We were to divide everything.

4
00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:23.640
Property and obligations.
- So what?

5
00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:30.800
We have a schedule.
Tonight is your turn to cook.

6
00:00:30.920 --> 00:00:34.280
Order a pizza.
Money is on kitchen table.

7
00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:43.240
DIVORCE IN PEACE

8
00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:57.520
Hey, what are you doing?
Why are you washing your teeth here?

9
00:00:57.640 --> 00:01:00.160
I have told you not to do that.
You don’t wash your teeth here.

10
00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:04.080
Foam is all over the place.

11
00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:09.720
We have to eat your foam later.
Why don’t you wash in the bathroom?

12
00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:15.280
What?
- Somebody’s clothes are in the bathtub.

13
00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:22.640
These are my clothes.
I’m sorting things for my travel.

14
00:01:22.760 --> 00:01:24.600
There’s also a sink.

15
00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:28.200
In the sink are mother’s things.
She was looking for make-up toner.

16
00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:29.760
What?

17
00:01:29.880 --> 00:01:33.080
You wouldn’t understand anyway.
- OK. Make-up.

18
00:01:35.720 --> 00:01:38.960
And I wouldn’t understand anyway.

19
00:01:41.080 --> 00:01:43.040
Right.

20
00:01:43.160 --> 00:01:46.600
What’s the problem if mother
wants to put make-up on again?

21
00:01:46.720 --> 00:01:48.560
She’s a single woman.

22
00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:54.040
Take it easy! Don’t goggle.

23
00:01:58.840 --> 00:02:03.720
A significant point in divorce
or let’s even say – a milestone –

24
00:02:03.840 --> 00:02:07.520
is when one of the partners
finds a new partner.

25
00:02:07.640 --> 00:02:10.240
Usually this doesn’t happen
simultaneously.

26
00:02:10.360 --> 00:02:14.160
One partner is always the first
to start a new relationship.

27
00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:18.560
Yes, but isn’t it too early
to discuss this? We are just…

28
00:02:18.680 --> 00:02:21.680
This may not happen tomorrow…
- Well, but…

29
00:02:21.800 --> 00:02:26.200
Tomorrow or not,
we have to speak about it.

30
00:02:26.320 --> 00:02:30.200
This situation may become
unexpectedly complicated.

31
00:02:30.320 --> 00:02:35.880
In our heart we want to take decisions.
Marriage inertia wouldn’t let go.

32
00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:38.320
Sometimes even after
they have been separated for years.

33
00:02:38.440 --> 00:02:42.720
I have no intention to interfere
if Aksel would find a new partner.

34
00:02:42.840 --> 00:02:44.320
Thank you!
- You’re welcome!

35
00:02:44.440 --> 00:02:46.960
Well, that is what many think.
In the beginning.

36
00:02:47.080 --> 00:02:50.520
But I have nobody else!
- We’ll keep this theoretical now.

37
00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:53.160
This “theoretical” is fine with us.

38
00:02:53.280 --> 00:02:56.080
Our marriage has been theoretical
for a very long time.

39
00:02:56.200 --> 00:02:59.360
What?

40
00:03:00.760 --> 00:03:02.520
Oh, I see.

41
00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:08.880
The trick is to learn to let go painlessly.
For us Estonians it’s very difficult.

42
00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:13.000
We can’t let go of anything,
neither good nor bad.

43
00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:21.160
So, the fourth therapy mission...
“Hello, this is my new life partner”.

44
00:03:23.160 --> 00:03:28.240
Role play. Laura will introduce
her new partner to Aksel

45
00:03:28.360 --> 00:03:31.160
and Aksel his partner to Laura.

46
00:03:31.280 --> 00:03:36.160
Where… How we…
- Let your friends to help you.

47
00:03:36.280 --> 00:03:39.840
Who?
- Maybe Tauno and Mirjam?

48
00:03:39.960 --> 00:03:42.200
What are you talking about!
It’s embarrassing.

49
00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:46.120
On the contrary!
That’s fine. And it’s useful.

50
00:03:49.320 --> 00:03:52.760
She is putting the make-up on?
Dolls up?

51
00:03:52.880 --> 00:03:59.440
Puts the make-up on for this rich man,
restaurant chain owner.

52
00:03:59.560 --> 00:04:00.840
Rihard Engel.

53
00:04:00.960 --> 00:04:03.640
She doesn’t have make-up on for me
for ages.

54
00:04:03.760 --> 00:04:07.680
We are taking each other for granted.

55
00:04:07.800 --> 00:04:11.000
Come on!
- No, let me speak.

56
00:04:11.120 --> 00:04:14.720
We were like two pieces of furniture
arranged randomly side by side.

57
00:04:16.200 --> 00:04:23.120
There were times when I went outside
to burp to avoid embarrassment.

58
00:04:23.240 --> 00:04:25.360
What kind of life is that!

59
00:04:25.480 --> 00:04:27.920
I had comb next to my bed.

60
00:04:28.040 --> 00:04:33.640
To comb my hair in the morning
to look better. Do you understand?

61
00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:38.440
Don’t weep! I’ll keep an eye
on this Rihard affair.

62
00:04:38.560 --> 00:04:42.200
Finally Laura has to admit honestly
what is going on.

63
00:04:42.320 --> 00:04:45.400
Laura is right, we have grown apart.

64
00:04:45.520 --> 00:04:48.320
Stop this growing apart talk!
It doesn’t apply any more,

65
00:04:48.440 --> 00:04:52.120
when she hooks up
a millionaire match by her side.

66
00:04:52.240 --> 00:04:55.320
Listen, one more thing.

67
00:04:55.440 --> 00:04:58.400
We have this therapy mission tonight.
- So?

68
00:04:58.520 --> 00:05:01.440
We are attending this therapy, right?
- Yes, so?

69
00:05:01.560 --> 00:05:04.040
Now we’ll need your help.
- Any time!

70
00:05:04.160 --> 00:05:08.720
I mean, Laura needs your help
and I’ll need Mirjam’s.

71
00:05:08.840 --> 00:05:09.840
And?

72
00:05:09.960 --> 00:05:12.880
The mission is that
we both have a new relationship

73
00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:15.720
and we have to introduce
our new partner.

74
00:05:16.720 --> 00:05:20.560
Laura will be more specific,
what she will need from you.

75
00:05:20.680 --> 00:05:23.960
We’ll meet at our place tonight.
We’ll offer food and drinks

76
00:05:24.080 --> 00:05:26.880
and we’ll work through this nonsense.

77
00:05:28.560 --> 00:05:31.000
Whoa! Wait.

78
00:05:31.120 --> 00:05:38.400
You would be Laura’s new partner
and Mirjam mine. Not for real.

79
00:05:38.520 --> 00:05:42.320
I see! You do that sort of things!

80
00:05:42.440 --> 00:05:44.960
It’s just a mission.
There are all kind…

81
00:05:45.080 --> 00:05:48.400
Laura is my new partner?
- Yes.

82
00:05:48.520 --> 00:05:56.240
Why not, let’s do it! What…
It’s… who else, but us!

83
00:05:56.360 --> 00:06:02.040
Of course. Mirjam and…
Mirjam! Come here!

84
00:06:02.160 --> 00:06:07.000
Put on your sexy underwear,
the green one.

85
00:06:07.120 --> 00:06:09.080
It’s not for real.

86
00:06:09.560 --> 00:06:14.240
The thing is we take each other
for granted.

87
00:06:14.360 --> 00:06:17.960
I don’t comb my hair often enough,
- My God, Aksel.

88
00:06:18.080 --> 00:06:24.360
In marriage it should be allowed
to take the other for granted.

89
00:06:24.480 --> 00:06:28.960
We’re here for each other always.
These are marriage principles.

90
00:06:29.080 --> 00:06:31.400
In sickness and in health,
with or without the comb.

91
00:06:31.520 --> 00:06:32.640
Who said that?

92
00:06:32.760 --> 00:06:36.760
Oh, God...! Already
the ancient Estonians lived like that.

93
00:06:36.880 --> 00:06:40.680
We are not a Rio Carnival folk
telling “I love you” every 5 seconds.

94
00:06:40.800 --> 00:06:43.800
How often Estonians should say
“I love you”?

95
00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:47.520
We do things differently,
more inward, in depth.

96
00:06:47.640 --> 00:06:52.960
Micro events, cosmic light flares.
Inward. - Really? That’s fascinating.

97
00:06:53.080 --> 00:06:57.160
Yes, fascinating. Your statement
that only you have contributed,

98
00:06:57.280 --> 00:06:59.960
this is really selfish and wrong thinking.

99
00:07:00.080 --> 00:07:03.280
Really?
But I have organised all this for us.

100
00:07:03.400 --> 00:07:06.440
I bought this house,
I paid the mortgage.

101
00:07:06.560 --> 00:07:10.400
Nothing is done in this house!
I’m at home creating atmosphere.

102
00:07:10.520 --> 00:07:13.080
What fucking atmosphere?
- You don’t even notice that!

103
00:07:13.200 --> 00:07:18.240
Let me guess. It’s a very Estonian,
inward thing? Invisible?

104
00:07:18.360 --> 00:07:21.680
You wouldn’t understand,
You simply wouldn’t understand.

105
00:07:22.920 --> 00:07:25.480
You’ll get half of everything.
I promised.

106
00:07:25.600 --> 00:07:27.400
You’ll get half of everything!

107
00:07:27.520 --> 00:07:30.840
I tell you, I don’t want this charity,
when you at the same time…

108
00:07:30.960 --> 00:07:35.320
What I at the same time?
- I want nothing, will live under a tree.

109
00:07:35.440 --> 00:07:39.800
Play a martyr! Right, a martyr!
- I’ll throw myself to the lions!

110
00:07:39.920 --> 00:07:44.360
Fine! First let’s do the therapy thing.
Tauno will be here any minute.

111
00:07:44.480 --> 00:07:47.360
You’ll go and talk with Mirjam.
- Already going...

112
00:07:47.480 --> 00:07:49.680
Where are you going?
Tauno will be here soon.

113
00:07:49.800 --> 00:07:52.320
We should have something on the table.
Are you going shopping?

114
00:07:52.440 --> 00:07:54.720
I’m not going.
- Exactly!

115
00:07:56.680 --> 00:07:59.440
Do I get it right
that I’m your girlfriend?

116
00:07:59.560 --> 00:08:08.880
Yes. We have to figure out where we met,
to make story credible, reliable.

117
00:08:09.000 --> 00:08:13.240
Then we’ll go to our house
and perform our roles.

118
00:08:13.360 --> 00:08:14.520
Really cool!

119
00:08:15.880 --> 00:08:20.000
I don’t know anymore what to do.
Does it make any sense?

120
00:08:20.120 --> 00:08:21.840
What do you mean by that?

121
00:08:23.280 --> 00:08:29.000
Me and Laura, we are sworn enemies…
we are enemies.

122
00:08:29.120 --> 00:08:33.560
How this role play would help?
Only rubs salt in our wounds.

123
00:08:34.480 --> 00:08:38.640
Listen, I think you simply have…
Look...

124
00:08:40.040 --> 00:08:44.960
There are these phases.
Attending therapy is sensible.

125
00:08:45.080 --> 00:08:51.760
You are having a phase radiating
these thoughts and emotions.

126
00:08:53.000 --> 00:08:56.800
This radiation hurts.

127
00:08:58.000 --> 00:09:03.240
You have to trust professionals.
- Well, yes.

128
00:09:03.360 --> 00:09:08.720
Dear Aksel, where did we meet?
- Well…

129
00:09:08.840 --> 00:09:12.360
In a club? On the beach?
In internet?

130
00:09:13.400 --> 00:09:20.320
I have never been to a club or beach.

131
00:09:20.440 --> 00:09:26.240
I use Internet but for other purpose.
It’s a little bit sordid.

132
00:09:26.360 --> 00:09:31.480
OK. Let’s think of something
realistic, but exciting.

133
00:09:31.600 --> 00:09:35.200
Right.
- Let’s have some encouragement.

134
00:09:35.320 --> 00:09:39.880
What do you mean?
- I have here some bubbly.

135
00:09:40.000 --> 00:09:45.960
Shouldn’t we be professional?
Does alcohol go with this?

136
00:09:46.080 --> 00:09:52.200
Pilots take a shot before taking off.
And all actors drink.

137
00:09:53.840 --> 00:09:59.760
So, the whole shebang, right?
In theory this should be fun.

138
00:09:59.880 --> 00:10:01.480
Fun?

139
00:10:03.240 --> 00:10:07.720
Why not? Let’s take this
as a relaxing party game.

140
00:10:07.840 --> 00:10:11.760
Relaxing divorce game?

141
00:10:11.880 --> 00:10:16.600
At wedding there are all kind of games,
why not during a divorce?

142
00:10:16.720 --> 00:10:21.080
We should come up with a cover story
how we met.

143
00:10:22.800 --> 00:10:25.880
Right. The cover story.

144
00:10:30.200 --> 00:10:35.240
Wait… I got cold feet.

145
00:10:35.360 --> 00:10:40.120
Let’s agree that you say nothing,
I’ll do all the talking. You just sit.

146
00:10:41.040 --> 00:10:45.960
Slow down, just slow down.
- Well?

147
00:10:47.640 --> 00:10:50.360
I don’t know if I’ll manage this.

148
00:10:50.480 --> 00:10:55.360
It’s totally against my real wishes.
What me and Mirjam…

149
00:10:55.480 --> 00:10:58.920
Can’t you set the things straight
in some other way? Why a divorce?

150
00:10:59.040 --> 00:11:03.120
Tauno, you promised to help
and not to meddle and interfere.

151
00:11:03.240 --> 00:11:04.640
All right.

152
00:11:04.760 --> 00:11:09.600
So, where did we meet?
The cover story. Where did we meet?

153
00:11:11.440 --> 00:11:13.040
We…

154
00:11:23.560 --> 00:11:28.200
Met in the art gallery?
- Yes, we met in the art gallery.

155
00:11:28.320 --> 00:11:34.160
No, that’s boring, very boring.
It’s not realistic. Me in gallery? No.

156
00:11:34.280 --> 00:11:36.960
It should be a place,
where I would go to.

157
00:11:38.600 --> 00:11:45.360
A party or a villa or a yoga event.
That would be fun! Tantra?

158
00:11:45.480 --> 00:11:48.320
I don’t know…
Eurovision after party?

159
00:11:48.440 --> 00:11:50.560
Wait, I wouldn’t go there!

160
00:11:50.680 --> 00:11:54.480
C’mon! You could. It’s a fantasy!
- All right.

161
00:11:54.600 --> 00:11:58.400
We were walking around
among all the people.

162
00:11:58.520 --> 00:12:04.920
Our eyes met. Our eyes met,
you clung to my eyes.

163
00:12:05.040 --> 00:12:12.520
I leaned toward you.
Your warm breath close to my face.

164
00:12:12.640 --> 00:12:19.320
I felt your heartthrob, your breath.
We lost our heads completely.

165
00:12:19.440 --> 00:12:21.440
Oh, dear God!

166
00:12:53.640 --> 00:13:01.920
And so, Aksel, may I introduce,
this is my new life partner Pierre.

167
00:13:04.480 --> 00:13:11.600
Pierre is a French cruise ship captain.
Are you all right?

168
00:13:11.720 --> 00:13:15.600
Sorry, I’ll manage.
Everything is all right.

169
00:13:17.240 --> 00:13:23.800
We met on the romantic cruise,
we both got a divorce recently.

170
00:13:27.480 --> 00:13:29.960
Tauno! Pierre...

171
00:13:36.320 --> 00:13:39.560
Maybe we should start?
- Okay.

172
00:13:41.360 --> 00:13:47.440
We had more realistic approach.
- Yes.

173
00:13:49.080 --> 00:13:53.040
Where did we meet, Aksel?

174
00:13:56.720 --> 00:14:02.960
My name is Monika.
I’m Aksel’s new neighbour.

175
00:14:03.080 --> 00:14:08.040
And?
- This bloody… I’ll…

176
00:14:11.240 --> 00:14:14.600
Aksel came to borrow some sugar.

177
00:14:14.720 --> 00:14:22.280
All developed very quickly.
One thing led to another.

178
00:14:22.400 --> 00:14:25.440
Bodies covered with sweat
close to each other

179
00:14:25.560 --> 00:14:33.320
and we rolled around in passion
and suddenly this all happened and…

180
00:14:33.440 --> 00:14:39.280
We stayed together.
- Yes, we developed a relationship.

181
00:14:39.400 --> 00:14:42.360
That’s really nice.
- What can I say!

182
00:14:44.600 --> 00:14:47.560
I still have some value on this market.

183
00:14:48.760 --> 00:14:50.760
Congratulations!

184
00:14:50.880 --> 00:14:57.480
Yes, from me too.
Congratulations! Sincerely.

185
00:15:19.240 --> 00:15:26.440
This was a strange experience.
- Thank you for helping.

186
00:15:26.560 --> 00:15:29.960
Any time. Any time.

187
00:15:36.360 --> 00:15:40.000
Our briefcase is full of missions
and we have managed none.

188
00:15:40.120 --> 00:15:45.080
Maybe all this divorce is wrong?
- No. We simply suck at this.

189
00:16:01.200 --> 00:16:07.520
Should I start packing
my bed linen and my clothes?

190
00:16:07.640 --> 00:16:11.640
You don’t have to do this right away.
You could find a rental for yourself.

191
00:16:11.760 --> 00:16:14.080
I will be dealing with house sell.
- Already?

192
00:16:14.200 --> 00:16:19.240
Property market is hot at the moment
and we will probably get a good deal.

193
00:16:19.360 --> 00:16:23.840
Odd types will be looking around here?
- Types will be looking around.

194
00:16:23.960 --> 00:16:30.200
Can Tauno and Mirjam have a say
on their new neighbours?

195
00:16:30.320 --> 00:16:32.480
Probably not.

196
00:16:32.600 --> 00:16:35.880
Is it fair to them?
- Life isn’t fair.

197
00:16:38.560 --> 00:16:43.760
We have been lucky to be so friendly
with our neighbours for 25 years.

198
00:16:43.880 --> 00:16:48.320
As one big family.
- As one family. Right.

199
00:16:51.360 --> 00:16:55.560
We’ll find normal people here.
More normal than us.

200
00:16:55.680 --> 00:16:59.120
That’s for sure!
- It wouldn’t be too complicated.

201
00:17:01.960 --> 00:17:05.160
Would you like me to help you
to pack and sort?

202
00:17:05.280 --> 00:17:08.040
No need. I’ll manage myself.
Perfectly!

203
00:17:10.080 --> 00:17:11.480
Okay.

204
00:17:16.200 --> 00:17:18.040
Yes, mother?

205
00:17:19.000 --> 00:17:21.240
What colloquium?

206
00:17:21.360 --> 00:17:25.360
Oh, dear God.
My parents are coming.

207
00:17:27.440 --> 00:17:31.840
Very good. Tell them to come.
At least somebody is worried about us.

208
00:17:31.960 --> 00:17:38.320
Hello, Aksel! Hello, dear daughter!
We came to try for the last time.

209
00:17:39.440 --> 00:17:44.760
We are still very worried
and haven’t accepted the situation.

210
00:17:44.880 --> 00:17:51.320
Exactly.
We can’t hide our heads in the sand.

211
00:17:51.440 --> 00:17:54.240
Estonians don’t behave like that.

212
00:17:54.360 --> 00:17:59.520
Now, I’ll talk to Laura.
- And dad will talk to you.

213
00:17:59.640 --> 00:18:01.160
Okay.
- Mother!

214
00:18:01.280 --> 00:18:03.760
Men between themselves!

215
00:18:04.920 --> 00:18:10.280
Dear daughter, I’m begging you,
reconsider. Let’s think together.

216
00:18:10.400 --> 00:18:15.320
We’ll help you to think.
What the life would be like?

217
00:18:16.000 --> 00:18:18.640
Alone in a flat somewhere.
It’s awful!

218
00:18:18.760 --> 00:18:20.720
Did Aksel call again to complain?

219
00:18:20.840 --> 00:18:27.920
No, no. It’s independent initiative
of grandparents’ colloquium.

220
00:18:28.040 --> 00:18:32.840
Mother, it’s my life, my feelings.
Nobody else can show the direction.

221
00:18:32.960 --> 00:18:37.080
But it’s not only your life.
That’s the point.

222
00:18:37.200 --> 00:18:44.480
If you would do this to poke Aksel,
so he would notice you.

223
00:18:44.600 --> 00:18:46.760
But you really want a divorce.

224
00:18:46.880 --> 00:18:53.840
Maybe I wanted to poke a little,
but then his affair came out.

225
00:18:55.120 --> 00:18:56.520
What?

226
00:18:56.640 --> 00:18:59.680
Oh mother, dear God.
I don’t want to talk about this.

227
00:18:59.800 --> 00:19:01.800
That’s not important right now.

228
00:19:01.920 --> 00:19:07.880
Not important! When your husband
has cheated on you? Laura!

229
00:19:08.000 --> 00:19:15.440
You have to behave like a man,
Don’t be such a wimp!

230
00:19:15.560 --> 00:19:21.240
A man doesn’t allow his wife
to be capricious, to have whims.

231
00:19:21.360 --> 00:19:23.880
What can I do?
We are not living in the Middle Ages.

232
00:19:24.000 --> 00:19:27.160
I can’t put a chastity belt on her
to lock her up in a castle!

233
00:19:27.280 --> 00:19:31.720
What chastity belt has to do with it?
Dear God! Chastity belt!

234
00:19:31.840 --> 00:19:34.840
She hasn’t cheated on you!
- Hasn’t she?

235
00:19:36.600 --> 00:19:41.120
What? What?
- No, it’s… isn’t…

236
00:19:41.240 --> 00:19:43.240
Spill it out!
- I don’t want to.

237
00:19:43.360 --> 00:19:44.720
Come on, tell.

238
00:19:44.840 --> 00:19:48.480
I’ll tell, but it's just between us.
- Promise!

239
00:19:49.440 --> 00:19:55.120
There’s a businessman, quite rich man.
Name is Rihard, not to mention names.

240
00:19:55.240 --> 00:19:57.880
Engel?

241
00:20:00.360 --> 00:20:02.840
Son of a bitch!

242
00:20:04.200 --> 00:20:08.960
Maybe it’s better
to get a friendly divorce.

243
00:20:10.680 --> 00:20:15.080
Daughter, I’m disappointed in you,
very disappointed.

244
00:20:16.120 --> 00:20:18.800
An Estonian woman
wouldn’t behave like this.

245
00:20:20.120 --> 00:20:24.360
Dad just needs some more time.
- As we all do.

246
00:20:24.480 --> 00:20:28.120
Someone has had
all the time in the world!

247
00:20:29.640 --> 00:20:34.280
What did you tell your mother about me?
- What did you tell my father about me ?

248
00:20:34.400 --> 00:20:37.040
I told as the things are.
- I told the same thing.

249
00:20:37.160 --> 00:20:38.960
All is well then.
- Right.

250
00:20:41.280 --> 00:20:42.920
"Mirjam: Let’s talk."

251
00:20:52.000 --> 00:20:53.880
Mirjam!

252
00:20:55.440 --> 00:20:59.640
Aksel.
- I wanted to say there’s no need to…

253
00:20:59.760 --> 00:21:03.000
What happened
was all wrong and unacceptable.

254
00:21:03.120 --> 00:21:05.120
This would never happen again.

255
00:21:07.160 --> 00:21:09.960
This role game turned unexpectedly…
- OK.

256
00:21:10.080 --> 00:21:15.800
OK? Can we forget this?
Be friends again? Dear God, Tauno.

257
00:21:15.920 --> 00:21:18.000
Tauno? Tauno has his toys.

258
00:21:18.120 --> 00:21:22.520
I’m under pressure these days.
This affects my judgement.

259
00:21:23.560 --> 00:21:26.000
I want you to know,
I have no regrets.

260
00:21:26.120 --> 00:21:29.800
And Tauno will not find out.

261
00:21:29.920 --> 00:21:33.000
You are a single man, in principle.
- Am I?

262
00:21:33.120 --> 00:21:34.840
Of course you are.

263
00:21:34.960 --> 00:21:39.520
It still a betrayal.
This shouldn’t happen again.

264
00:21:39.640 --> 00:21:42.280
If Tauno will find out,
he will shoot me.

265
00:21:42.400 --> 00:21:44.320
Calm down!

266
00:21:45.640 --> 00:21:48.880
Aksel, I was thinking
about us in the evening.

267
00:21:49.000 --> 00:21:53.720
Wait, Mirjam. It’s serious.
- He will go to training assembly soon.

268
00:21:53.840 --> 00:22:00.280
I wanted to say that if you want
to talk about us, to relax a little,

269
00:22:00.400 --> 00:22:03.800
you’ll know where to find me.
Right?

270
00:22:03.920 --> 00:22:07.400
I thought, on the contrary, Mirjam...

271
00:22:19.400 --> 00:22:21.360
Aksel!
- Tauno!

272
00:22:21.480 --> 00:22:23.280
Let’s talk.
- Yes?

273
00:22:25.160 --> 00:22:29.560
What you and Mirjam did yesterday…
- Tauno, no, no. It was really…

274
00:22:29.680 --> 00:22:37.120
You played your roles so well.
Sorry that I failed.

275
00:22:37.240 --> 00:22:39.880
No, no. It was…

276
00:22:40.000 --> 00:22:46.000
Your divorce. I still can’t believe
that it’s really happening.

277
00:22:46.120 --> 00:22:48.880
Yes, well… It’s…

278
00:22:49.000 --> 00:22:53.360
Let’s remain friends, right?
No matter what. Friends till the end.

279
00:22:53.480 --> 00:22:55.360
Yes, no matter what.

280
00:23:00.640 --> 00:23:04.840
You are right. It’s my life.

281
00:23:04.960 --> 00:23:10.360
No one tells us how to live our life.
Men have decided for women far too long.

282
00:23:10.480 --> 00:23:12.360
Right!

283
00:23:12.480 --> 00:23:17.440
Your courage makes me
to reassess what’s important.

284
00:23:17.560 --> 00:23:19.400
What do you mean?

285
00:23:19.520 --> 00:23:22.960
I’m talking about Tauno.
Are we compatible?

286
00:23:23.080 --> 00:23:26.680
Maybe all this is only a habit?

287
00:23:26.800 --> 00:23:33.840
Wait! I don’t want to undermine
your life with my problems.

288
00:23:33.960 --> 00:23:38.080
No, no. I can see it now.
That’s how I feel.

289
00:23:40.440 --> 00:23:41.720
I see.

290
00:23:41.840 --> 00:23:45.760
Can’t you match it?
Maybe mom is doing this on purpose?

291
00:23:45.880 --> 00:23:52.320
Make-up and new clothes.
Do the same, make mom jealous.

292
00:23:52.440 --> 00:23:54.120
How?

293
00:23:54.240 --> 00:23:59.680
How? Look at yourself!
Fix yourself up!

294
00:24:01.760 --> 00:24:07.080
Cut these pyjamas off.
Ask Tauno. He's got the angle grinder.

295
00:24:07.200 --> 00:24:11.240
What are you talking about?
Stop it!

296
00:24:11.360 --> 00:24:15.960
Mother would be pleased
if I would go out and find somebody.

297
00:24:16.080 --> 00:24:19.200
She would be pleased
and would feel less guilty.

298
00:24:19.320 --> 00:24:22.840
But you don’t know that.
A woman is not a counting table.

299
00:24:22.960 --> 00:24:25.040
Slide beads and get an answer...

300
00:24:25.160 --> 00:24:27.600
Woman is a complicated
metaphysical creature.

301
00:24:27.720 --> 00:24:32.520
And what a man is?
Big pile of stinking sweaty physics?

302
00:24:32.640 --> 00:24:36.400
Go to a night club.
Who knows what will happen!

303
00:24:37.600 --> 00:24:41.480
This is insane. I’m a violin teacher.
Dear God!

304
00:24:52.920 --> 00:24:54.720
Jesus, dad!

305
00:24:54.840 --> 00:24:59.000
This is water, not a… It’s water.

306
00:25:03.160 --> 00:25:04.800
It’s water!

307
00:25:18.680 --> 00:25:22.760
Mirjam called me.
Things are getting serious.

308
00:25:22.880 --> 00:25:25.560
Well. I… I’ll tell you, that…

309
00:25:25.680 --> 00:25:29.080
Mirjam wants to sit down
and to have a talk tonight.

310
00:25:29.200 --> 00:25:32.520
To examine our marriage.
To value, to consider.

311
00:25:32.640 --> 00:25:39.040
This divorce thing is like a bush fire,
as infectious disease, domino effect.

312
00:25:39.160 --> 00:25:40.800
Sorry! Shit!

313
00:25:40.920 --> 00:25:46.680
All was fine with us, right?
Except that I can’t have children.

314
00:25:46.800 --> 00:25:53.680
Yes, but that’s not decisive.
She only wants to talk with you.

315
00:25:54.760 --> 00:25:59.840
I don’t have to worry.
Of course!

316
00:26:04.280 --> 00:26:07.840
I looked through your divorce papers.
All is really fair.

317
00:26:07.960 --> 00:26:11.600
Laura has been fair in dealings.
Equal parts.

318
00:26:11.720 --> 00:26:15.400
Easy to be fair and flash money around,
when your new man is a millionaire!

319
00:26:15.520 --> 00:26:20.720
It’s not easy to sell one’s business.

320
00:26:20.840 --> 00:26:26.480
Listen. I thought I will not demand
this bakery. I’m above it.

321
00:26:26.600 --> 00:26:30.320
What? Accept this offer.
You have to rebuild your life somehow.

322
00:26:30.440 --> 00:26:32.160
Well, yes.

323
00:26:35.440 --> 00:26:37.640
We trust each other, right?

324
00:26:38.520 --> 00:26:48.560
If there’s one man in this world
I’ll trust, then it’s you, Aksel.

325
00:26:51.120 --> 00:26:55.440
Tauno, I have to tell you something.

326
00:27:01.520 --> 00:27:06.840
The same here. Exactly.
From my side total confidence.

327
00:27:08.240 --> 00:27:10.320
Thank you, friend!

328
00:27:18.200 --> 00:27:21.720
Mona, 100 thousand viewers!

329
00:27:33.960 --> 00:27:38.080
Where are you going?
- Do you want to know?

330
00:27:41.440 --> 00:27:46.720
It’s natural for a wife to be interested,
where the husband is going at night.

331
00:27:48.520 --> 00:27:52.120
So, where the husband is going?
- To a night club.

332
00:27:53.600 --> 00:27:56.120
You?
- Yes, me.
